WEBVTT

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:04.460
It's the sixth day of the inter-high.

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:06.250
Stage A's third game is currently in

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:08.310
East Hand 4, Bonus 1 of the first half

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:10.090
of the fourth players' match.

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:13.240
The dealer is Atago Kinue.

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:14.240
Pon!

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:28.710
Pon!

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:55.030
<b>The Nationals</b>

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:08.840
Usuzumi from Eisui Girls' calls,

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:11.670
<b>Hand 8: 
Fortress</b>

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:11.900
bringing a nervous air to the table.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:22.640
East Hand 4

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:22.640
Carried Bonus 1
 Dealer: Atago Kinue

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:26.750
<i>The North-East Gate of Evil?</i>

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:31.930
Calling on the North and East 
while she's the north player...

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.800
Usuzumi Hatsumi does that remarkably often.

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:39.510
North and East?

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:44.560
She puts the North and East tiles 
in the North-East Gate of Evil,

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:50.060
and then she'll start getting 
the South and West tiles.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:52.730
Southwest.

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:54.320
That is to say...

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.070
<i>The South-West Gate of Evil.</i>

00:02:57.790 --> 00:03:00.240
<i>They're already in her hand...</i>

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:08.000
<i>If it's like our teacher said, 
then if this continues on...</i>

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:11.530
<i>If she wins, it doesn't matter 
if it's by tsumo or not.</i>

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:13.360
<i>We'll be in last place.</i>

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:16.620
<i>I can't let her play freely!</i>

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.260
<i>They're coming!</i>

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:24.180
<i>They're all coming to me!</i>

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:51.180
<i>What is this?!</i>

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:03.230
<i>Is this girl for real?</i>

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:08.930
You need to watch out 
for Miyamori's Usuzawa.

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:11.520
Why?

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:14.660
Have you ever heard of 
Mekaru, from Okinawa?

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:16.290
No.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:19.640
You know, the girl from Niraikanai.

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:24.930
That Mekaru didn't win a hand 
in the first round match.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:27.240
Not once in two East-South matches.

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:30.670
In the Iwate preliminaries,

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:35.170
the opponents Usuzawa had marked 
were unable to win their hands.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:39.800
She seals the hand of those 
she looks at? Is that it?

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:45.930
I don't know, but be cautious of her, 
especially when you're the north player.

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:50.710
<i>My tiles really did stop coming!</i>

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:54.940
<i>I can't believe I can't win 
while being the north player.</i>

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:58.790
<i>No, no, that can't be!</i>

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:00.690
<i>Fine, then take this!</i>

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:05.650
Ron. 11,900.

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:08.030
<i>No way...</i>

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:12.280
<i>She played into her hand on purpose?</i>

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:16.580
<i>Another hand as the north player?!</i>

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:18.980
<i>Is she just planning on playing into</i>

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:21.090
<i>the dealer's hand until she wins herself?</i>

00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:25.210
<i>You're going to destroy yourself!</i>

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:32.850
Good luck, Sae!

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:38.060
Will Miyamori's fourth player go as we expected?

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:39.590
I think...

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:42.820
she will.

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:49.570
No tenpai.

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:52.990
Looks like I'm not the dealer anymore.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.820
Now for the South round.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:59.250
South Hand 1

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:59.250
Carried Bonus 3

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:07.760
It looks like she managed to 
hold her back the first time.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.470
South Hand 3

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:13.600
Tenpai!

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:15.730
No tenpai here.

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:16.930
No tenpai.

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:17.680
No tenpai.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:20.840
<i>All right.</i>

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:23.360
<i>I'm the dealer again.</i>

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:25.530
<i>Which also means that</i>

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:28.530
<i>Usuzumi's the north player.</i>

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:31.780
<i>East and North?</i>

00:06:32.110 --> 00:06:33.200
That's right.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:35.720
If she calls on either one of those,

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:39.420
don't discard the other 
until she can no longer call.

00:06:39.890 --> 00:06:42.620
So if she calls on the East, 
I shouldn't discard the North,

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:45.430
and if she calls on the North, 
I shouldn't discard the East.

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:47.170
Is that what you mean?

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:51.730
This only applies if Eisui's Usuzumi 
happens to be the north player.

00:06:51.730 --> 00:06:54.140
The other schools will 
probably also get in her way.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:55.810
That's all it'll take,

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:58.690
<i>and the fourth match will be yours, Kinu-chan.</i>

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:02.310
First half, South Hand 4

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:02.310
Carried Bonus 1

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:06.070
Last dealer: Atago Kinue

00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:10.950
Pon on that!

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:15.870
<i>I guess the first one is fine.</i>

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:17.350
<i>As long as the East doesn't 
make an appearance,</i>

00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:18.950
<i>I have no reason to be afraid.</i>

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:29.380
Pon on that, too!

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:35.890
<i>Kiyosumi... I thought it was just 
a mistake during the East round,</i>

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:38.150
<i>but you seriously don't 
know about this, do you?</i>

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:42.260
<i>Kiyosumi is hopeless.</i>

00:07:42.260 --> 00:07:45.210
<i>I've got no choice. 
I guess I'll block it.</i>

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:49.050
<i>That's if you can do it!</i>

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:51.530
<i>Now, come to me,</i>

00:07:53.980 --> 00:07:55.320
<i>South and West!</i>

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:16.120
<i>Has she completely sealed me again?</i>

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:20.890
<i>Then I'll go for a honitsu.</i>

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:24.020
Ron!

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:26.760
6,700.

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:32.650
The first half of the fourth 
players' match is over!

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:41.450
Eisui Girls' (Kagoshima)
 Fourth Player - 3rd Year
 Usuzumi Hatsumi

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:39.730
Unexpectedly, the seed school 
Eisui Girls' Usuzumi Hatsumi

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:41.450
has lost a lot of points!

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:47.960
Himematsu High School 
(South Osaka)
 Fourth Player - 2nd Year
 Atago Kinue

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:44.390
Himematsu High School is still in first place.

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:47.960
The younger sister widens the 
lead that her sister achieved.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:53.970
Kiyosumi High School (Nagano)
 Fourth Player - 1st Year
 Haramura Nodoka

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:51.470
The inter-middle champion, Haramura Nodoka,

00:08:51.470 --> 00:08:53.970
gained a few points and maintained 2nd place.

00:08:54.010 --> 00:09:02.600
Miyamori Girls' (Iwate)
 Fourth Player - 3rd Year
 Usuzawa Sae

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:56.690
Miyamori Girls' is in 3rd.

00:08:56.690 --> 00:09:00.140
While their position hasn't changed, 
they have lost a few points.

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:02.600
We can expect them to turn 
it around in the second half.

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:05.300
<i>This is rough.</i>

00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:08.060
<i>This is on par with what it 
was like going against Toyone.</i>

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:12.160
<i>If it was just one more hand, 
I could maybe do it.</i>

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:16.570
<i>But Kiyosumi's just totally oblivious...</i>

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:20.860
<i>This might end badly.</i>

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:26.080
Sae!

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:31.340
Sae!

00:09:31.850 --> 00:09:33.440
What are you looking at?

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:34.490
Kurumi...

00:09:35.990 --> 00:09:37.570
Here, umbrella.

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:38.870
Thanks.

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:43.060
You heard that a new teacher is coming,

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:45.390
supposedly an old friend of the principal's, right?

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:48.440
No, I hadn't heard. Now?

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:49.190
Yes.

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:52.690
I'm pretty sure that person 
was on the train that just passed.

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:54.900
You must've been imagining it!

00:09:56.230 --> 00:09:57.530
Even if I was,

00:09:59.970 --> 00:10:02.710
I don't think it was a bad thing to imagine.

00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:37.620
Oh, it's rare to see you sitting at the table.

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:38.730
No...

00:10:39.930 --> 00:10:43.590
After I sat down, I got so 
tired, I couldn't get up.

00:10:45.590 --> 00:10:46.450
I see.

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:48.860
Where's Kurumi?

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:50.460
She's coming later.

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:53.370
Oh, that was quick.

00:10:57.420 --> 00:10:59.800
So I see you do have a table.

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:01.450
Who are you?

00:11:01.900 --> 00:11:03.560
Kurumi aged...

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:06.310
<i>This feeling...</i>

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:11.730
Could you be the new...

00:11:12.030 --> 00:11:15.810
I will start teaching at Miyamori Girls' next week.

00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:17.480
My name is Kumakura Toshi.

00:11:17.810 --> 00:11:19.340
<i>I knew it!</i>

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:21.850
Why did you come to this room?

00:11:21.850 --> 00:11:24.240
Did you get lost because 
the campus is so big?

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:26.140
No, no.

00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:28.840
My hobby is mahjong,

00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:32.530
so my feet naturally carry me 
toward where the tiles are.

00:11:32.530 --> 00:11:34.580
That's handy for when you've lost a tile.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:38.090
Do you feel like playing a little bit now?

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:42.790
Right now? We don't have four players.

00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:44.010
I'm tired.

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:45.790
I'm back!

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:47.540
Who is that?!

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:48.970
Now we have four.

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:03.480
Tsumo.

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:08.030
8,700 all.

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:13.920
<i>This lady...</i>

00:12:14.450 --> 00:12:16.420
Looks like that's eight in a row.

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:19.670
<i>Is she really a teacher?!</i>

00:12:48.840 --> 00:12:51.700
Tsumo. 6,800 all.

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:53.530
Aww!

00:12:53.530 --> 00:12:55.460
Looks like everybody went bust again.

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:59.960
But it was fun to play with four 
players for the first time in so long.

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:02.720
You only have three club members?

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:04.570
Unfortunately.

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:07.090
I see.

00:13:08.740 --> 00:13:13.600
I took a bit of a detour on my way here,

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:17.480
and I found an interesting girl on the way.

00:13:23.590 --> 00:13:27.210
I think I'd like to introduce her to you.

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:32.930
Sae...

00:13:33.690 --> 00:13:34.750
Sae!

00:13:36.570 --> 00:13:37.750
Sae!

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:42.890
Are you okay?

00:13:46.020 --> 00:13:47.010
Shiro...

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:50.140
I was sleeping.

00:13:50.460 --> 00:13:51.760
Want me to lend you one?

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:53.720
What?

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:55.100
A hand or a shoulder.

00:13:56.890 --> 00:14:01.360
I'm fine. I'd be done for if 
I had to let you nurse me.

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:06.570
But to think that you'd leave 
the waiting room to come find me.

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:09.380
I was on my way to go pee...

00:14:09.380 --> 00:14:11.620
So you didn't come because 
you were worried?!

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:15.220
You know, you should pay 
lip service there, even if it's a lie.

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:16.580
Don't be shy about it.

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:17.320
Ti—

00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:18.080
Ti?

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:19.520
Nothing.

00:14:40.780 --> 00:14:42.000
Thanks for waiting.

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:43.460
Did you calm down?

00:14:43.460 --> 00:14:44.270
Yep.

00:14:50.520 --> 00:14:54.280
Earlier, I remembered...

00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:59.400
when the teacher first came to our club room.

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:04.310
Back then, we both happened to 
be in the club room, remember?

00:15:04.860 --> 00:15:06.480
Were we?

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:07.340
Yeah.

00:15:10.100 --> 00:15:14.730
Back then, we only had three club members...

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:16.130
Yeah.

00:15:21.830 --> 00:15:25.670
But now we have five.

00:15:32.540 --> 00:15:34.030
Sometimes I think to myself.

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:40.040
Did our teacher know that 
this was going to happen?

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:41.700
Foresight?

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:45.130
No, not quite something like that.

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:49.200
But it was always just the three of us.

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:52.050
We don't get many new students, either.

00:15:53.390 --> 00:15:58.570
I thought I'd end up graduating 
before anything changed.

00:16:00.070 --> 00:16:03.850
That's why I don't want it to 
end here, no matter what.

00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:08.900
Just a little longer...

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:14.320
For just a little longer...

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:16.490
I want us five to be together.

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:25.920
Good luck.

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:29.900
Well, it'll be a piece of cake.

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:40.220
The break is over and the players 
have returned to the stage.

00:16:41.030 --> 00:16:42.500
The South round of the first half

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:45.910
didn't have any big moves 
in this fourth players' match.

00:16:45.910 --> 00:16:48.980
The second half is just about to begin.

00:16:58.030 --> 00:17:01.490
Miyamori Girls' (Iwate)
 Fourth Player - 3rd Year
 Usuzawa Sae

00:17:01.490 --> 00:17:05.000
Eisui Girls' (Kagoshima)
 Fourth Player - 3rd Year
 Usuzumi Hatsumi

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:08.500
Kiyosumi High School 
(Nagano)
 Fourth Player - 1st Year
 Haramura Nodoka

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:12.010
Himematsu High School 
(South Osaka)
 Fourth Player - 2nd Year
 Atago Kinue

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:21.010
And the second half of the 
fourth players' match has begun!

00:17:21.410 --> 00:17:25.020
<i>Since we're seated differently, 
Usuzumi is suddenly the north player.</i>

00:17:25.800 --> 00:17:27.890
<i>If Kiyosumi was the last dealer,</i>

00:17:27.890 --> 00:17:29.520
<i>I could have rested a bit.</i>

00:17:34.180 --> 00:17:35.130
Riichi.

00:17:40.390 --> 00:17:41.280
<i>Seriously?</i>

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:43.000
<i>A dealer riichi?</i>

00:17:48.760 --> 00:17:49.750
Chi.

00:17:57.960 --> 00:17:58.680
Pon.

00:18:04.460 --> 00:18:05.180
Pon.

00:18:06.460 --> 00:18:08.910
<i>Damn it, Kiyosumi!</i>

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:11.190
<i>I have no choice but to block it again.</i>

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:14.940
<i>No calling to take the tsumo win for herself?</i>

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:18.680
<i>No siphoning of luck or 
anything weird like that?</i>

00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:21.990
<i>She crushes her opponent's 
win just by looking at them?</i>

00:18:23.210 --> 00:18:26.080
<i>There's no way that can be real!</i>

00:18:34.020 --> 00:18:35.090
I'm back.

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:36.820
Welcome back.

00:18:36.820 --> 00:18:38.090
You took a long time.

00:18:40.860 --> 00:18:43.100
How is Sae?

00:18:44.280 --> 00:18:47.620
You went to see her, right?

00:18:50.340 --> 00:18:52.630
She was saying it'll be a piece of cake.

00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:55.360
And what's your verdict?

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:58.610
She looked exhausted.

00:19:01.760 --> 00:19:04.580
I was the one who lent that to her

00:19:04.850 --> 00:19:07.330
so she wouldn't waste her power needlessly,

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:10.940
but using it to seal her opponents

00:19:10.940 --> 00:19:13.960
is something she's doing with her own power.

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:18.300
The stronger the opponent she seals,

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:21.220
the more stress it puts on her.

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:25.480
And Kiyosumi's dragging her down, too! Right?

00:19:25.480 --> 00:19:27.000
Way down!

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:31.310
Haramura-san is digital,

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:33.990
so I think she's doing the right thing.

00:19:33.990 --> 00:19:35.770
You're right.

00:19:36.190 --> 00:19:40.950
Discarding honor tiles is commonplace nowadays.

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:44.530
But that that is making Sae suffer is also fact.

00:19:47.410 --> 00:19:51.040
I wonder how long Sae's spirit will last...

00:19:53.530 --> 00:19:54.640
Tenpai.

00:19:54.640 --> 00:19:55.590
Tenpai.

00:19:55.590 --> 00:19:56.630
No tenpai.

00:19:56.630 --> 00:19:57.500
No tenpai.

00:19:59.140 --> 00:20:00.920
<i>I'm at the end of my rope here,</i>

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:03.800
<i>but Usuzumi is still the north player.</i>

00:20:10.780 --> 00:20:12.220
Nodoka.

00:20:12.220 --> 00:20:15.190
In the second round match, 
you need to watch out for suushiihou.

00:20:17.080 --> 00:20:19.120
I don't quite get what you mean.

00:20:19.120 --> 00:20:21.170
I figured you'd say that.

00:20:21.170 --> 00:20:22.570
But I wanted to let you know.

00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:27.400
If there's someone calling 
on East and North,

00:20:27.400 --> 00:20:30.490
and you don't know where 
West and South are,

00:20:30.490 --> 00:20:32.100
then it wouldn't hurt to consider

00:20:32.100 --> 00:20:34.570
the possibility of a yakuman, right?

00:20:35.530 --> 00:20:37.210
Maybe a little...

00:20:40.570 --> 00:20:43.750
Though, I think the probability 
that someone can always

00:20:43.750 --> 00:20:46.340
call East and North when 
they're the north player

00:20:47.480 --> 00:20:50.100
is lower than coincidence.

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:54.810
Second Half
East Hand 1
Bonus 1

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:54.810
Dealer: Haramura Nodoka

00:21:07.510 --> 00:21:10.030
<i>I have no East or North tiles in my hand.</i>

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:14.290
<i>There are none in the discards, either.</i>

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:19.040
<i>Usuzumi probably has a pair of both 
North and East tiles in her hand.</i>

00:21:19.450 --> 00:21:22.590
<i>Kiyosumi is bent on following her style,</i>

00:21:22.590 --> 00:21:25.050
<i>so she will discard them if she has any.</i>

00:21:25.650 --> 00:21:28.510
<i>I just hope Himematsu 
can keep hers to herself.</i>

00:21:41.330 --> 00:21:44.260
<i>Kiyosumi is going to discard the 
second one without any thought,</i>

00:21:44.260 --> 00:21:47.490
<i>so that makes it hard to discard 
the first East and North...</i>

00:21:50.070 --> 00:21:50.740
Ron.

00:21:54.760 --> 00:21:56.330
9,900.

00:21:56.740 --> 00:21:59.830
<i>Chiitoitsu? That was ready?</i>

00:22:01.550 --> 00:22:02.810
Bonus 2.

00:22:04.010 --> 00:22:05.920
<i>A dealer renchan...</i>

00:22:06.950 --> 00:22:13.450
<i>Then that means Usuzumi will be 
the north player again... yet again!</i>

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:49.860
<b>Next time:</b>

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:49.860
<b>Sortie</b>

00:23:36.090 --> 00:23:38.190
When someone follows my 
riichi with another riichi,

00:23:38.190 --> 00:23:40.380
I feel like I often lose. 
I wonder if that's accurate.

00:23:40.380 --> 00:23:41.460
You're just imagining it.

00:23:41.460 --> 00:23:45.340
That feeling probably comes from having 
memories of dealing into their hands.

00:23:45.340 --> 00:23:47.950
Nodo-chan never wavers!

00:23:49.860 --> 00:23:55.000
<b>You better</b>

00:23:49.860 --> 00:23:55.000
<b>watch again!</b>
